      "hints": [
        "From $y = a + b\\sin x$, $y$-intercept is $a = -2$ and peak is $a + b = 1 \\implies b = 3$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Identify key features from the sine graph $y = a + b\\sin x$:\n- At $x = 0$, $y = a + b\\sin(0) = a = -2$\n- At $x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$, the maximum value is $y = a + b = 1 \\implies -2 + b = 1 \\implies b = 3$\n$$a = -2, \\quad b = 3$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
