      "hints": [
        "Factorise $(3\\cos\\theta + 1)(\\cos\\theta - 1) = 0 \\implies \\cos\\theta = 1, -\\frac{1}{3}$.",
        "Solve in $[-180^\\circ, 180^\\circ]$ to find $\\theta = -109.5^\\circ, 0^\\circ, 109.5^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factorise the quadratic in $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$(3\\cos\\theta + 1)(\\cos\\theta - 1) = 0 \\implies \\cos\\theta = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\cos\\theta = -\\frac{1}{3}$$",
        "Find the solutions for $\\theta$ in the range $-180^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 180^\\circ$:\n$$\\text{For } \\cos\\theta = 1: \\quad \\theta = 0^\\circ$$\n$$\\text{For } \\cos\\theta = -\\frac{1}{3}: \\quad \\theta = \\pm\\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\approx \\pm 109.47^\\circ \\approx \\pm 109.5^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = -109.5^\\circ, \\quad 0^\\circ, \\quad 109.5^\\circ)$$"
      ],
